    {
      "sentence_id": 3,
      "arabic_di": "كَانَ يَجْلِسُ عَلَى حَافَّةِ السَّرِيرِ وَهَاتِفُهُ مَقْلُوبٌ عَلَى الطَّاوِلَةِ الصَّغِيرَةِ بِجَانِبِهِ، وَكُوبُ الشَّايِ الَّذِي أَحْضَرَتْهُ لَهُ أُمُّهُ قَبْلَ سَاعَةٍ قَدْ بَرَدَ تَمَامًا دُونَ أَنْ يَلْمَسَهُ.",
      "transliteration": "Kāna yajlisu ʿalā ḥāffat al-sarīr wa-hātifu-hu maqlūb ʿalā al-ṭāwilah al-ṣaghīrah bi-jānibihi, wa-kūb al-shāy alladhī aḥḍarat-hu la-hu ummuh qabla sāʿah qad barada tamāman dūna an yalmisah.",
      "english": "He was sitting on the edge of the bed, his phone face-down on the small table beside him, and the cup of tea which his mother had brought him an hour ago had gone completely cold without him touching it.",
